Let $n - 1 > 0$ be an integer. Find all sequences $a_{1}, a_{2}, \ldots, a_{n^{2}+n}$ satisfying the following conditions:
(a) $a_{i} \in \{0,1\}$ for all $1 \leq i \leq n^{2}+n$;
(b) $a_{i+1}+a_{i+2}+\ldots+a_{i+n} < a_{i+n+1}+a_{i+n+2}+\ldots+a_{i+2n}$ for all $0 \leq i \leq n^{2}-n$.

For every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ let $d(n)$ denote the number of (positive) divisors of $n$. Find all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ with the following properties:
(i) $d(f(w))=w$ for all $w \in \mathbb{N}$;
(ii) $f(w y)$ divides $(w-1) y^{w y-1} f(w)$ for all $w, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

negatives.text:
Let $d(n)$ denote the number of positive divisors of $n$ for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$. Find all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ such that:
(1) $d(f(x)) = x$ for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(2) $f(x y)$ divides $(x + 1) y^{x y - 1} f(x)$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

Let $d(n)$ denote the number of positive divisors of $n$ for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$. Find all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ such that:
(1) $d(f(x)) = x$ for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(2) $f(x y)$ divides $(x - 1) y^{x y} f(x)$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

Let $d(n)$ denote the number of positive divisors of $n$ for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$. Find all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ such that:
(1) $d(f(x)) = x$ for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(2) $f(x y)$ divides $(x - 1) y^{x y - 1} f(y)$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

