Two circles $C_1$ and $C_2$, with centres at $D$ and $E$ respectively, touch at $B$. The circle having $DE$ as diameter intersects the circle $C_1$ at $H$ and the circle $C_2$ at $K$. The points $H$ and $K$ both lie on the same side of the line $DE$. $HK$ extended in both directions meets the circle $C_1$ at $L$ and meets the circle $C_2$ at $M$. Prove that
(a) $\left|{H L}\right| - \left|{K M}\right| = 0$;
(b) the line through $B$ perpendicular to $DE$ bisects $HK$.

negatives.text:
Two circles $C_1$ and $C_2$, with centres at $D$ and $E$ respectively, intersect at $B$. The circle with diameter $DE$ intersects $C_1$ at $H$ and $C_2$ at $K$, both on the same side of $DE$. $HK$ extended intersects $C_1$ at $L$ and $C_2$ at $M$. Prove that
(a) $|LH| = |KM|$;
(b) the line through $B$ perpendicular to $DE$ bisects $HK$.

Two circles $C_1$ and $C_2$, with centres at $D$ and $E$ respectively, touch at $B$. The circle with diameter $DE$ intersects $C_1$ at $H$ and $C_2$ at $K$, with $H$ and $K$ on opposite sides of $DE$. $HK$ extended intersects $C_1$ at $L$ and $C_2$ at $M$. Prove that
(a) $|LH| = |KM|$;
(b) the line through $B$ perpendicular to $DE$ bisects $HK$.

Two circles $C_1$ and $C_2$, with centres at $D$ and $E$ respectively, touch at $B$. The circle with diameter $DE$ intersects $C_1$ at $H$ and $C_2$ at $K$, both on the same side of $DE$. $HK$ extended intersects $C_1$ at $L$ and $C_2$ at $M$. Prove that
(a) $|LH| < |KM|$;
(b) the line through $B$ perpendicular to $DE$ bisects $HK$.

Sia $h$ un numero intero positivo e sia $a_{n}$ definita come:
$$
\begin{aligned}
 a_{0} & =1 \\
 a_{n+1} & = \begin{cases}
 \frac{a_{n}}{2} & \text{ se } a_{n} \text{ è pari } \\
 a_{n}-h & \text{ se } a_{n} \text{ è dispari.}
\end{cases}
\end{aligned}
$$

(Ad esempio, se $h=27$ si ha: $a_{1}=28, a_{2}=14, a_{3}=7, a_{4}=34, a_{5}=17, a_{6}=44, \ldots$)

Per quali valori di $h$ esiste $n>0$ per cui $a_{n}=1$ ?

