Problem:

How many functions $f: \mathbb{Z} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ satisfy the following three properties?
(a) $f(1)=1$;
(b) For all $w, u \in \mathbb{Z}$, $f(w)^2 - f(u)^2 = f(w+u) f(w-u)$;
(c) For all $u \in \mathbb{Z}$, $f(u) = f(u+2013)$.

negatives.text:
